# tpot2cti — Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Per LESSONS_LEARNED §9.1: minimize the build context so layer-cache
# invalidations only happen when source actually changes.  Without this
# file, every `git status` artifact and stray log/db invalidates COPY.

# --- VCS ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Python caches ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Runtime data (gitignored too; never bake into an image) ---
data/
logs/
ssh-keys/
*.duckdb
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# --- Docs (large, not needed at runtime) ---
docs/
V1_SPEC.md
README.md
*.md
!LICENSE

# --- Sibling compose projects (sidecars have their own contexts) ---
tpot2cti-credentials/
tpot2cti-vault/
tpot-tunnel/
opencti/

# --- Compose / scripts / tooling not needed inside the core image ---
docker-compose*.yml
setup.sh
teardown.sh
update.sh
Makefile

# --- Editor / OS ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
